        },
        {
          "label": "Mechanisms (Components of Drain)",
          "children": [
            { "label": "Home Charges: Pensions and salaries of British officials in London, interest on public debt, cost of military purchases in England." },
            { "label": "Profits of foreign enterprises sent back; cost of expanding the British empire outside India paid from Indian revenues." },
            { "label": "Impact: Severe capital erosion preventing industrialisation; chronic poverty and low per capita income." },
            { "label": "**Significance**: The Drain Theory provided a powerful intellectual justification for the demand for Swaraj." }
