            { "label": "Mountbatten Plan (3 June 1947): Accepted the inevitability of partition.\nOrdered the division of Punjab and Bengal; mandated referendums in NWFP and Sylhet district (Assam).\nAlso set the date of independence as 15 August 1947." },
            { "label": "**Analysis**: Mountbatten's acceleration of the timeline was controversial; some argue it was necessary to avoid civil war, others claim it was a hasty abdication of responsibility." }
          ]
        },
