                "label": "TRAP: Regarded as first step toward representative institutions, but did NOT introduce elections; legislative council had no power over finance or executive control",
                "kind": "trap"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "label": "Indian Councils Act 1892",
            "kind": "subsection",
            "children": [
              {
                "label": "Legislative functions expanded: could discuss budget, ask questions (6 days notice), but no supplementary questions or voting on budget",
                "kind": "bullet"
