    "label": "Making of the Constitution & Sources",
    "kind": "section",
    "children": [
      {
        "label": "Constituent Assembly & Objectives Resolution",
        "kind": "subsection",
        "children": [
          {
            "label": "Demand, Formation & Composition",
            "kind": "subsection",
            "children": [
              {
                "label": "Concept first put forward by M.N.\nRoy (1934); officially demanded by INC in 1935; accepted in principle via August Offer (1940)",
                "kind": "bullet"
              },
              {
                "label": "Formed Nov 1946 under Cabinet Mission Plan; provinces allotted seats in ratio of 1 seat per million population",
                "kind": "fact"
              },
              {
                "label": "TRAP: Partly elected, partly nominated; members were indirectly elected by members of Provincial Legislative Assemblies using single transferable vote proportional representation",
                "kind": "trap"
              },
              {
                "label": "Total strength 389 (292 elected from British provinces + 93 nominated from princely states + 4 from chief commissioners' provinces); after Partition and withdrawal of Muslim League, reduced to 299 (229 provinces + 70 princely states)",
                "kind": "bullet"
              },
              {
                "label": "TRAP: Mahatma Gandhi and M.A.\nJinnah were NOT members of the Constituent Assembly",
                "kind": "trap"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "label": "Proceedings, Key Figures & Committees",
            "kind": "subsection",
            "children": [
              {
                "label": "First meeting: Dec 9, 1946; Dr.\nSachchidananda Sinha chosen as temporary President (French practice); Dec 11: Dr.\nRajendra Prasad elected permanent President; H.C.\nMukherjee and V.T.\nKrishnamachari elected as two Vice-Presidents",
                "kind": "case"
