              {
                "label": "Jawaharlal Nehru moved Objectives Resolution on Dec 13, 1946; unanimously adopted on Jan 22, 1947; modified version became the Preamble",
                "kind": "bullet"
              },
              {
                "label": "TRAP: Under Indian Independence Act 1947, the Assembly became a fully sovereign body and assumed dual functions: (1) Constituent body chaired by Dr.\nRajendra Prasad, (2) Legislative body chaired by G.V.\nMavlankar",
                "kind": "trap"
              },
              {
                "label": "Important functionaries: B.N.\nRau (Constitutional Adviser; not a member), Prem Behari Narain Raizada (Calligrapher, italic style), Nand Lal Bose and Beohar Rammanohar Sinha (Decorators/Illuminators), Elephant (Seal), H.V.R.\nIengar (Secretary), S.N.\nMukherjee (Chief Draftsman)",
                "kind": "bullet"
              },
              {
                "label": "Drafting Committee (appointed Aug 29, 1947): B.R.\nAmbedkar (Chairman), N.\nGopalaswami Ayyangar, Alladi Krishnaswamy Ayyar, Dr.\nK.M.\nMunshi, Syed Mohammad Saadullah, N.\nMadhava Rau (replaced B.L.\nMitter), T.T.\nKrishnamachari (replaced D.P.\nKhaitan)",
