                "label": "TRAP: Amending acts add new articles as sub-clauses (e.g., 21A, 51A); the original numbering structure up to Art 395 remains structurally intact",
                "kind": "trap"
              },
              {
                "label": "Partly rigid, partly flexible: three methods of amendment (simple majority, special majority, special majority + state ratification)",
                "kind": "amendment"
              },
              {
                "label": "Federal in structure, unitary in spirit.\nQuotes: K.C.\nWheare ('quasi-federal'), Morris-Jones ('bargaining federalism'), Granville Austin ('cooperative federalism'), Ivor Jennings ('federation with a strong centralising tendency'), Paul Appleby ('extremely federal')",
