      "difficulty": "hard"
    },
    {
      "id": "cm-final-007",
      "q": "Consider the following statements regarding the membership of the Chief Minister in the State Legislature: 1. A person who is not a member of either House can be appointed as Chief Minister for a maximum of six consecutive months. 2. A Chief Minister who belongs to the State Legislative Council cannot vote in a no-confidence motion against his own government. 3. The Constitution mandates that a non-member CM must be elected specifically to the State Legislative Assembly, not the Council, within six months. How many of the above statements are correct?",
