      "answer": "B",
      "difficulty": "mid"
    },
    {
      "id": "cm-final-008",
      "q": "Consider the following statements regarding the relationship between the Chief Minister and the Governor: 1. The Chief Minister holds office during the pleasure of the Governor. 2. The Governor can dismiss the Chief Minister at any time if the Governor subjectively feels the CM has lost the confidence of the people. 3. The question whether any, and if so what, advice was tendered by the CM to the Governor cannot be inquired into in any court. How many of the above statements are correct?",
      "options": { "A": "Only one", "B": "Only two", "C": "All three", "D": "None" },
      "answer": "B",
      "difficulty": "hard"
    },
    {
      "id": "cm-final-009",
      "q": "Consider the following bodies: 1. Inter-State Council 2. Governing Council of NITI Aayog 3. National Integration Council. In how many of the above bodies does the Chief Minister of a state serve as a member?",
