    {
      "id": "cm-final-011",
      "q": "Consider the following statements regarding the resignation of the Chief Minister: 1. The resignation of the Chief Minister automatically results in the resignation of the entire Council of Ministers. 2. When a CM resigns, the Governor is constitutionally bound to dissolve the Legislative Assembly. 3. A caretaker Chief Minister appointed by the Governor retains full constitutional powers to take major policy decisions. How many of the above statements are correct?",
