      "q": "Consider the following statements regarding the Advocate General of the State: 1. The Chief Minister advises the Governor on the appointment of the Advocate General. 2. The Advocate General holds office during the pleasure of the Chief Minister. 3. The remuneration of the Advocate General is determined by the State Legislature on the recommendation of the Chief Minister. How many of the above statements are correct?",
      "options": { "A": "Only one", "B": "Only two", "C": "All three", "D": "None" },
      "answer": "A",
      "difficulty": "hard"
    },
    {
