      "q": "Consider the following statements regarding the Chief Minister's role in the State Legislature: 1. The Chief Minister advises the Governor with regard to summoning and proroguing the sessions of the State Legislature. 2. The Chief Minister can recommend the dissolution of the Legislative Assembly to the Governor at any time. 3. The Chief Minister is the principal channel of communication between the Governor and the State Legislature. How many of the above statements are correct?",
