      "answer": "B",
      "difficulty": "easy"
    },
    {
      "id": "cm-final-015",
      "q": "Consider the following statements: 1. The Chief Minister swears an oath of office and secrecy, which is administered by the Chief Justice of the respective High Court. 2. The oath of secrecy taken by the Chief Minister is identical to the oath of secrecy taken by a Union Cabinet Minister. 3. The Governor cannot administer the oath to the Chief Minister if the Governor is functioning in an acting capacity. How many of the above statements are correct?",
