  "topic": "Comptroller and Auditor General (CAG) – Final 110% Set",
  "difficultyTag": "H",
  "mcqs": [
    {
      "id": "cag-final-001",
      "q": "Consider the following statements regarding the 'Comptroller' aspect of the CAG's office: 1. The CAG of India has the constitutional power to authorize the withdrawal of money from the Consolidated Fund of India. 2. Unlike the British CAG, the Indian CAG has no control over the issue of money from the exchequer. 3. The Indian CAG conducts the audit strictly after the expenditure has already taken place. How many of the above statements are correct?",
