      "q": "Consider the following statements regarding the co-option of members to the board of a cooperative society: 1. The board may co-opt a maximum of two persons having specialized experience in banking, management, finance, or specialization in any other related field. 2. These co-opted members must be counted within the constitutional upper limit of twenty-one directors. 3. The co-opted members enjoy full voting rights, including the right to vote in the election of the chairperson of the cooperative society. How many of the above statements are correct?",
      "options": { "A": "Only one", "B": "Only two", "C": "All three", "D": "None" },
      "answer": "A",
      "difficulty": "hard"
