      "q": "Consider the following statements regarding the supersession or suspension of the board of a cooperative society: 1. Generally, a board can be kept under supersession or suspension for a maximum period of six months. 2. If the cooperative society is carrying on the business of banking, the maximum period of supersession can extend to one year. 3. In the case of a cooperative bank, the supersession of the board must be done after mandatory consultation with the Reserve Bank of India (RBI). How many of the above statements are correct?",
      "options": { "A": "Only one", "B": "Only two", "C": "All three", "D": "None" },
      "answer": "C",
      "difficulty": "mid"
