        "C": "Both served 2 terms",
        "D": "M. Venkaiah Naidu (1 term)"
      },
      "answer": "C",
      "difficulty": "easy"
    },
    {
      "id": "polity-vice-president-149",
      "q": "The Vice-President, while discharging the President's functions, is not entitled to:",
      "options": {
        "A": "The salary and allowances of the President",
        "B": "The title of 'President'",
        "C": "The immunities of the President",
        "D": "He is entitled to all of the above"
      },
      "answer": "D",
      "difficulty": "mid"
    },
    {
      "id": "polity-vice-president-150",
      "q": "The Vice-President's office is a constitutional office. The Constitution provides for his election in Article:",
      "options": {
        "A": "63",
        "B": "66",
        "C": "67",
        "D": "68"
      },
      "answer": "B",
      "difficulty": "hard"
    },
    {
      "id": "polity-vice-president-151",
      "q": "The Vice-President is the ex-officio Chairman of Rajya Sabha. This means:",
      "options": {
        "A": "He is automatically the Chairman without any separate election",
        "B": "He is elected separately as Chairman",
        "C": "He can be removed from Chairmanship without losing Vice-Presidentship",
        "D": "He can resign from Chairmanship while remaining Vice-President"
      },
      "answer": "A",
      "difficulty": "mid"
    },
    {
      "id": "polity-vice-president-152",
      "q": "The Vice-President can exercise the President's powers when the President is unable to. This includes the power to:",
      "options": {
        "A": "Issue ordinances",
        "B": "Grant pardons",
        "C": "Declare emergencies",
        "D": "All of the above"
      },
      "answer": "D",
      "difficulty": "mid"
    },
    {
      "id": "polity-vice-president-153",
      "q": "The Vice-President, when acting as President, is subject to the same limitations as the President. He must act on the advice of:",
      "options": {
        "A": "The Prime Minister only",
        "B": "The Council of Ministers",
        "C": "His own discretion",
        "D": "The Supreme Court"
      },
      "answer": "B",
      "difficulty": "mid"
    },
    {
      "id": "polity-vice-president-154",
      "q": "The Vice-President is elected for a term of five years. The election to the office of Vice-President must be completed:",
      "options": {
        "A": "Before the expiration of the term of the outgoing Vice-President",
        "B": "Within three months of the vacancy",
        "C": "Within six months of the vacancy",
        "D": "Whenever the President decides"
      },
      "answer": "A",
      "difficulty": "easy"
    },
    {
      "id": "polity-vice-president-155",
      "q": "The Vice-President's office is not subordinate to the President. He is:",
      "options": {
        "A": "Independent and holds a constitutional office",
        "B": "Subordinate to the President",
        "C": "Under the Prime Minister",
        "D": "Subordinate to the Speaker"
      },
      "answer": "A",
      "difficulty": "mid"
    },
    {
      "id": "polity-vice-president-156",
      "q": "The Vice-President can be removed by a resolution passed by Rajya Sabha. This resolution requires:",
      "options": {
        "A": "A simple majority of members present",
        "B": "An absolute majority of the total membership",
        "C": "A two-thirds majority of members present and voting",
        "D": "A majority of the elected members"
      },
      "answer": "B",
      "difficulty": "easy"
    },
    {
      "id": "polity-vice-president-157",
      "q": "The Vice-President's election is held by proportional representation by single transferable vote. This system ensures:",
      "options": {
        "A": "That the winning candidate secures a majority of first-preference votes",
        "B": "Representation of minorities",
        "C": "A direct mandate",
        "D": "Both A and B"
